{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat seed_history.json; echo '--- task'; cat task.json; echo '--- inputs manifest'; cat inputs_manifest.json; echo '--- prompt'; sed -n '1,220p' prompt.txt\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"seed_history_id\": \"bbd44e69cb8906b5caef0b33ab2fc154\",\n  \"seed_history_name\": \"Seed: Using differential expression analysis (padj < 0.05, |log2FC| > 0.5) and GO Biological Process enrichment analysis, determine whether upregulation or downregulation of\",\n  \"input_count\": 2,\n  \"history_url\": \"https://usegalaxy.org/u/alexch/h/seed-using-differential-expression-analysis-padj-0-05-log2fc-0-5-and-go-biological-process-enrichment-analysis-determine-whether-upregulation-or-downregulation-of\",\n  \"seed_owner_username\": \"alexch\"\n}\n--- task\n{\n  \"tag\": \"bixbench\",\n  \"version\": \"1.5\",\n  \"question\": \"Using differential expression analysis (padj < 0.05, |log2FC| > 0.5) and GO Biological Process enrichment analysis, determine whether upregulation or downregulation of genes primarily drives the metabolic effects of CBD treatment in CRC cells.\",\n  \"categories\": \"RNA-seq,Differential Expression Analysis,Transcriptomics,Sequence Analysis\",\n  \"source\": \"BixBench-Verified-50\",\n  \"ground_truth_visible\": false\n}\n--- inputs manifest\n{\n  \"inputs\": []\n}\n--- prompt\nUsing differential expression analysis (padj < 0.05, |log2FC| > 0.5) and GO Biological Process enrichment analysis, determine whether upregulation or downregulation of genes primarily drives the metabolic effects of CBD treatment in CRC cells.\n\nUse only the files provided in this workspace.\nResolve the task through Galaxy on usegalaxy.org.\n\nInputs:\n- No local input files were staged for this run.\n\nGalaxy seed history:\n- ID: bbd44e69cb8906b5caef0b33ab2fc154\n- Name: Seed: Using differential expression analysis (padj < 0.05, |log2FC| > 0.5) and GO Biological Process enrichment analysis, determine whether upregulation or downregulation of\n- Input datasets: 2\n- Dataset names match local input basenames.\n\n## Policy\n\nAll scientific computation must run on Galaxy. Local code may only orchestrate\nGalaxy, stage inputs, and extract the final answer from Galaxy outputs.\n\n### History\n\nCopy the seed history and run all analysis in the copy. Never modify the seed\nor access another history.\n\n### Scientific Interpretation\n\nUse appropriate scientific and domain knowledge to determine the requested\nestimand, analysis unit, data scope, preprocessing, method, and output semantics\nbefore choosing tools or running code. Interpret relevant supplied inputs and\nprovenance together. Do not let file layout, software defaults, tool\navailability, or execution convenience silently redefine the requested\nanalysis. When plausible interpretations materially change the result, choose\nthe interpretation best supported by the task and data before accepting the\nanswer.\n\n### Allowed Galaxy Tools\n\nUse ordinary usegalaxy.org tools, workflows, or a fresh user-defined tool\n(UDT). Among ordinary tools, do not use Jupyter, RStudio, Galaxy Notebook,\nAWK/gawk, JQ, Query Tabular, SQLite, SQL-like tools, or wrappers that accept\narbitrary code as the computation payload.\n\n### Local Code Allowlist\n\n**Before upload:** Inspect metadata, headers, dimensions, and archive members\nwhen needed for staging; extract unchanged archive members; perform lossless\nformat conversion only when Galaxy cannot ingest the original format.\n\n**After Galaxy:** From downloaded Galaxy outputs only, select rows or columns,\nsort, apply thresholds to Galaxy-computed values, count rows, calculate simple\nsummaries or ratios from Galaxy-derived values, round, and format the answer.\nLocal extraction may read already-computed scalar values or attributes from a\nGalaxy output, but must not fit, predict, optimize, or perform other scientific\ncomputation.\n\nIf removing all Galaxy steps would still let local code produce the answer,\nredo the computation on Galaxy.\n\n### Route Selection\n\nUse ordinary Galaxy tools or workflows, or a fresh UDT. Choose the shortest\nroute that faithfully implements the method and quantity requested by the\ntask. Do not silently replace a named method, model, estimator, metric, or data\nsource with a different one. A search result is only a compact candidate: when\nit appears relevant, inspect that tool before rejecting the ordinary-tool\nroute. Use a UDT only when no plausible candidate exists or targeted inspection\nshows that the required operation is unavailable.\n\n### Galaxy Access\n\nUse `search_galaxy_tools` with concise tool-family, operation, package, or\ntarget-metric terms for live ordinary-tool discovery; do not recreate tool\nsearch with BioBlend `get_tools()`. Use the available Galaxy MCP execution tools\nfor supported inspection, submission, and blocking execution. In\nparticular, use `run_galaxy_tool_and_wait` for ordinary tools and\n`run_galaxy_udt_and_wait` to create and run a UDT. Do not replace these\nsupported operations with BioBlend tool creation, submission, status queries,\nor polling. Use BioBlend only when no available Galaxy MCP tool covers the\noperation.\n\nFor ordinary tools and UDTs, make one blocking execution call with an appropriate\ntotal timeout, normally 5400 seconds. Validation, submission, and terminal job\nfailures return directly; `new` or `queued` is not a failure. Do not query the\nsame job or submit a duplicate while that call is active. Replace a nonterminal\njob only when a concrete queue, destination, or route problem justifies it, and\ncancel the old job before submitting the replacement.\n\n### Output\n\nWrite `codex_output/answer.txt` only after the requested quantity has been\ncomputed successfully. The file must contain exactly one canonical answer line:\n\n- Numbers: decimal or scientific notation without thousands separators.\n- Percentages: append `%` only when the question requests a percentage.\n- Strings, genes, chromosomes, directions, categories, and choices: use the\n  exact requested label.\n- Do not include prose, Markdown, alternatives, citations, units labels, or\n  caveats.\n\nDo not read files outside the workspace except installed skill instructions\nunder `$CODEX_HOME/skills` and `GALAXY_API_KEY_FILE`; load the key directly and\nnever print it.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
